## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ICA pipeline design on real-world-like sensor data, including preprocessing, component selection, and robust evaluation. It also probes familiarity with common ICA algorithms and stability considerations across seeds.

## Key Concepts
- Centering and scaling inputs
- Whitening (PCA) before ICA
- Choosing n_components and nonlinearity
- Noise robustness and stability across seeds
- Evaluation with SDR/SIR against ground truth

## Code Example
```javascript
// ICA pipeline skeleton (pseudocode)
const X = [/* 2 x N data */];
const Xc = demeanAndScale(X);
const Xw = whiten(Xc);
const ica = new FastICA({nComponents:2, nonlinearity:'logcosh'});
const S = ica.fitTransform(Xw);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this pipeline if the mixing is time-varying?
- How would you detect and handle outliers that distort independence estimates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical online ICA pipeline under real-time constraints and nonstationary audio. It also probes decisions about whitening, joint diagonalization, and permutation under resource limits, plus simple robustness and evaluation plan.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening with forgetting factor
- Joint diagonalization vs per-bin ICA
- Cross-bin permutation using magnitude/phase cues
- Outlier handling for impulsive wind noise
- Embedded latency constraints
- Ground-truth based evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
for (let t of frames) {
  const X = STFT(t)
  const W = updateWhitening(X, α)
  const Y = Demix(W, X)
  const P = alignPermutation(Y)
  const Z = IFFT(P * Y)
  output(Z)
}
```

